\begin{align*}
\text{Area of trapezoid }ABCD &= \frac{1}2 \cdot \text{(sum of bases)} \cdot \text{(height)} \\
&= \frac{1}2 \cdot (10 + 12) \cdot 12 \\
&= \frac{1}2 \cdot 22 \cdot 12 \\
&= 132
\end{align*}

Next, notice that in order to calculate the areas of $ABYX$ and $XYCD$, we must first notice that $OY = \frac{1}2 \cdot \text{(base)}= \frac{1}2 \cdot 12 = 6$, giving $AY = 6$.

